{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persistent CI inspection error prevents the factory from observing later PRs in the repository."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When main is red, distinct PR failures are recorded with generic signatures instead of their actual errors and runner images."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A repository casing mismatch blocks CI classification and can repeatedly stop observation of later PRs."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun ending in a skipped or neutral conclusion remains unresolved and is inspected repeatedly."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A lost rerun response leaves an accepted retry unreconciled, so its passing result and flake evidence are lost."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later workflow attempt can prevent the factory from finding and recording an earlier rerun result, although the real API listing behavior remains unverified."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Multiple red checks produce separate repository alerts, though the evidence does not establish that per-check alerts violate the requested behavior."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unchanged PR failure suppressed while main is red never receives its retry or needs-fix classification after main recovers."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A cancelled matrix sibling can be recorded as failed then passed, though retrying current-head cancellations follows the stated policy."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If GitHub rejects a rerun while sibling jobs are running, the factory can consume the retry allowance without performing a retry, but that API restriction is unverified."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The two additive migrations apply successfully in order and their separation only adds maintenance churn."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun outside the first 100 observed contexts can remain unreconciled when its completion does not change the visible CI state."},{"id":"C16","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A tracked closed PR can emit a CI failure notification without the new classification, although its intended applicability to closed PRs is disputed."},{"id":"C17","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"Long setup output can displace the failure from the feed excerpt, while the separate signature still identifies the error."},{"id":"C18","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The configuration guide omits the default-enabled switch for automatic CI reruns."},{"id":"C19","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"An ordinary action input can be mistaken for the failure line, merging distinct failures and their retry allowances."},{"id":"C20","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Pending checks on a newer main commit clear the prior red state, allowing PR reactions before the new main result is known."}]}